3.1 Literacy
Literacy is defined as the ability to read
and write a short text in Dzongkha,
English, Lhotshamkha, or any other lan-
guage, while literacy rate is defined as the
ratio of literate population aged 6 years
and above to the total population of the
same age group expressed in percentage.
Out of 20,336 population aged 6 years
and above 15 persons had not responded
to the literacy questions. The literacy rate
for the Dzongkhag is, therefore, based on
a total population of 20,321 persons. The
